From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lenOS hardening <hardening@lenos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Connectivity bpf: enforce NETWORK permission in inet_create socket hook

Adds BPF_PERMISSION_NETWORK (1 << 5) and requires both INTERNET and NETWORK
bits before allowing AF_INET/AF_INET6 socket creation. This is the kernel-level
enforcement that makes the NETWORK permission (GrapheneOS second layer) actually
block sockets — the part a userspace firewall cannot do.

The default for a uid not present in uid_permission_map changes from
BPF_PERMISSION_INTERNET to (INTERNET | NETWORK), so the permission is
default-granted (normal|instant) and only bites when explicitly revoked.

Bit must match NetworkPermissions.TRAFFIC_PERMISSION_NETWORK (Java, 1 << 5).

HARD DEPENDENCY: this is the BPF half; it is only meaningful together with
fwb-0001 (permission declaration), connectivity-0001 (ConnectivityService
check), connectivity-0002 (bit + grant). Applying this ALONE with a stale
userspace would default-grant NETWORK (harmless) but not revoke it (incomplete).

NOT compiled/verified here (no Android build environment).
---
diff --git a/bpf/progs/netd.h b/bpf/progs/netd.h
--- a/bpf/progs/netd.h
+++ b/bpf/progs/netd.h
@@ -200,6 +200,9 @@
 enum BpfPermissionMatch : uint8_t {
     BPF_PERMISSION_INTERNET = 1 << 2,
     BPF_PERMISSION_UPDATE_DEVICE_STATS = 1 << 3,
+    // lenOS: NETWORK permission (second, revocable layer over INTERNET).
+    // Must match NetworkPermissions.TRAFFIC_PERMISSION_NETWORK (Java).
+    BPF_PERMISSION_NETWORK = 1 << 5,
 };
 // In production we use two identical stats maps to record per uid stats and
 // do swap and clean based on the configuration specified here. The statsMapType
diff --git a/bpf/progs/netd.c b/bpf/progs/netd.c
--- a/bpf/progs/netd.c
+++ b/bpf/progs/netd.c
@@ -784,8 +784,9 @@
      */
     uint32_t appId = uid % AID_USER_OFFSET;  // == PER_USER_RANGE == 100000
     uint8_t* permissions = bpf_uid_permission_map_lookup_elem(&appId);
-    // if UID not in map, then default to just INTERNET permission.
-    return permissions ? *permissions : BPF_PERMISSION_INTERNET;
+    // if UID not in map, then default to INTERNET + NETWORK (NETWORK is
+    // default-granted and revocable; see NetworkPermissions.java).
+    return permissions ? *permissions : (BPF_PERMISSION_INTERNET | BPF_PERMISSION_NETWORK);
 }
 
 static __always_inline inline int inet_socket_create(struct bpf_sock* sk,
@@ -795,7 +796,10 @@
         if (v) v->cookie = bpf_get_sk_cookie(sk);
     }
     uint64_t uid = bpf_get_current_uid_gid() & 0xffffffff;
-    if (get_app_permissions(uid) & BPF_PERMISSION_INTERNET) {
+    const uint8_t perms = get_app_permissions(uid);
+    // lenOS NETWORK permission: require BOTH INTERNET and NETWORK bits. Revoking
+    // NETWORK (while INTERNET stays) blocks socket creation -> app has no network.
+    if ((perms & BPF_PERMISSION_INTERNET) && (perms & BPF_PERMISSION_NETWORK)) {
         return bpf_owner_firewall_match(uid) == PASS ? BPF_ALLOW : BPF_DISALLOW;
     } else {
         return BPF_DISALLOW;
